feedback.message:
Defect 4 (Ball creation after losing life - one-frame visual glitch):

When the player loses a life (ball falls below canvas), a new ball is created at a fixed position in the "balls.length === 0" block (around line 561):
  balls = [makeBall(CANVAS_SIZE / 2, CANVAS_SIZE - 60)];

This creates the ball at (320, 580) regardless of paddle position. The gameState is then set to "idle", and in the next frame the gameState === "idle" block would set the ball to follow the paddle. But there is a one-frame delay where the ball appears at the fixed position (320, 580) instead of following the paddle.

Expected behavior: The new ball should be created at the paddle's current position (paddle.x + paddle.w / 2, paddle.y - ball.r), matching the idle-state ball-following behavior. This ensures visual consistency - the ball should always appear attached to the paddle before launch, whether it's the initial ball or a ball after losing a life.

The fix should change line 561 from:
  balls = [makeBall(CANVAS_SIZE / 2, CANVAS_SIZE - 60)];
to:
  balls = [makeBall(paddle.x + paddle.w / 2, paddle.y - 7)];

Similarly, the initial ball creation in resetPlay() at line 444 should also follow the paddle:
  balls = [makeBall(paddle.x + paddle.w / 2, paddle.y - 7)];

This would ensure the ball always appears attached to the paddle in idle state, which is the expected Breakout behavior.
